            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sissy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making this sauce for years. First of all, I would double the recipe, second combine all ingredients in a sauce pan and bring to boil, the heat intensify the flavor, especially the garlic. I keep tasting it and adding more fish sauce, lime juice and sugar as needed until I like it. Doing it this way, you also dissolve all the sugar, so the sugar wouldn't just settle to the bottom."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "4.3.20 Followed this recipe to the letter, and just didn’t care for the way it turned out. Very, very bland, weak flavor, and it just tasted like too much water…period! I would recommend that you start with 1/2 cup water, taste, and then add more if you feel it’s necessary. I did have some Thai chili peppers in the fridge, so I ended up slicing them and adding to the sauce to give it a little zing. Sorry for the less than favorable review, but this just didn’t work for me.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-03T18:59:05.937Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KADEZKO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Don't follow the instructions. Just mortar three red chilies with a tablespoon of garlic and add lemon juice and fish sauce to taste. Done.",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-20T19:32:19.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kelly Kindle Cheney"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Since it won't let me edit my review I will add another one. The second time I made this I thickened with corn starch stirred into part of the water. We liked it better this way. Bring to a boil until thickened.",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-17T16:12:05.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patrik Sova"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Too much water compared to other ingredients and too little lime juice compared to fish sauce and sugar. My Vietnamese girlfriend loves this version: 5 tablespoon sugar, 5 tablespoon fish sauce, 1 cup boiled water, 3 bird eye chilies, 3 cloves of garlic and 5 tablespoon fresh lime juice.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-26T16:07:35.718Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nguyen78"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A good start. I found that heating the water in the microwave for 30 secs or so helped the sugar dissolve more easily. I added 1/4 cup more water and a pinch less garlic. Can substitute Sriracha hot sauce for red pepper flakes.",
            "datePublished": "2010-09-27T09:27:55.023Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "momma mia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is awesome! but,not surprising considering it has everything I love, Garlic and fish sauce! Not to sweet. I did add 1 tbs garlic pepper paste. Will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-27T01:03:56.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jana_kink"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not exactly what the restaurant gives you but the closest I have found. I always heat mine up to dissolve the sugar. just on low in a pot while everything else is being prepped. Might try a little less fish sauce next time",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-05T20:54:51.453Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
